+.. rst:directive:: .. py:type:: name
+
+   Describes a type alias. The optional ``canonical`` option describes the
+   type represented by the alias and is displayed in the signature after an
+   equals sign. Its expression is parsed as a type annotation, so referenced
+   types use normal Python-domain cross-reference resolution. The directive
+   may also have a description body, but object directives cannot be nested
+   inside it.
+
+   .. rubric:: options
+
+   .. rst:directive:option:: canonical
